Independent phylogenetic test of the metal identity and grouping of 11 K04564
(Fe/Mn-SOD) transcripts recovered from four coral hosts' Symbiodiniaceae
symbionts (orbicella, pseudodiploria, siderastrea). The tree uses only the
conserved mature domain, so it is independent of both the metal-residue
fingerprint and the DeepLoc/leader-based localization analysis. Pipeline: MAFFT
L-INS-i alignment → trimAl -gappyout (438 → 185 columns; divergent N-terminal
leaders and insertions removed) → IQ-TREE ModelFinder (best model WAG+R4 by
BIC), 1000 ultrafast bootstrap + 1000 SH-aLRT replicates, midpoint-rooted.
Reference panel: 21 Fe + 21 Mn UniProt-annotated SODs (balanced by cofactor),
plus same-KO red-algal, brown-algal, and diatom sequences and the Lingulodinium
polyedra FeSOD (Q9AXR7, the proposed dual-target case).

Result. The 11 transcripts are monophyletic and split into the same two groups
the leader/DeepLoc analysis found. Group A (3 secreted/Extracellular
transcripts) forms a tight clade (SH-aLRT 99.9 / UFBoot 100) whose nearest
annotated homolog is a green-algal (Chlamydomonas) Mn-SOD — concordant with the
fingerprint's Mn call. Group B (8 Plastid/Unassigned transcripts) is sister to
two diatom Fe-SODs (Phaeodactylum tricornutum, Eolimna minima; containing clade
UFBoot 100) within a stramenopile Fe-SOD neighborhood — which conflicts with
the fingerprint's Mn call. Long-branch attraction was checked and ruled out
(symbiont tip branches are short, median 0.005 vs 0.092 subs/site for
references); Fe and Mn references segregate into a few strong local blocks (4
Fe↔Mn transitions across tip order), so neighborhood placement is informative.

Interpretation for annotation. Group A → Mn-SOD (two independent lines agree,
~85% confidence). Group B → metal unresolved: label conservatively as
"Fe/Mn-type SOD, fingerprint Mn vs. phylogeny Fe-neighborhood," not Mn on the
fingerprint alone. The two methods measure different things (metal-coordinating
residues vs. whole-domain ancestry) and Fe/Mn-SODs switch metal among close
homologs, so neither is decisive here. The tie-breaking test is to score the
canonical Fe-vs-Mn specificity/discriminant residues of Group B against the
diatom Fe-SODs and the Mn references at those columns specifically.

sod_phylogeny.png — annotated ML tree; Fe refs red, Mn refs blue, 11 symbiont
transcripts shaded and bracketed into Groups A and B; UFBoot ≥80 shown.

symb_phylo_grouping.tsv — per-transcript group assignment, fingerprint metal,
nearest annotated tree neighbor and its metal.

sod_ML.treefile — Newick tree with SH-aLRT/UFBoot support values.

sod_alignment_trimmed.faa — 185-column trimAl-trimmed mature-domain alignment
the tree was inferred from.
